From cd063849fde13ee92461cfdd6ab9554ff75a86de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:19:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 131/162] fix: the sky did not follow the aperture - the fog
 painting it was never exposed

User: in Manual, f/64 ISO 50 1/5000 ND10 blackens the ground and leaves the sky
bright; r_HDRDebug 1 with Spot on the sky reads a band of 1.08e6..1.24e6 cd/m2
"absolute" at EV 20. AUTO with sky in frame ran to its EV ceiling and the ground
went black; Sky Weight (5f1d292f) only masked that.

Root cause. The Nishita dome at CSkyStage HAS carried the pre-exposure since S1,
and r_SceneReferredNishitaScale 0.37 is applied on every dome recompute. But with
e_VolumetricFog 1 (the gamesdk project default) the sky texels at the far plane
are painted by the volumetric fog's ANALYTICAL segment,
GetVolumetricFogAnalyticalColor - from the ray-march volume's far edge to the
target, which for the sky is the whole optical path - and its sun colour,
PB_VolumetricFogScatteringColor / SecondaryColor (= GetSunColor() x fog albedo,
filled on the main thread in sGetVolumetricFogScatteringColor), never took the
exposure. S8 exposed the ray-marched half (SunColor, VolumetricFog.cpp) and the
research note claimed the legacy-fog multiply at VolumetricFog.cfi:154 covered
the analytical half; it is a different function. So the sky region of the frame
sat at a constant ~0.9 exposed units at every aperture: the meter divided that
by the exposure and reported 1.1e6 cd/m2, and no EV could move it.

Fix. The latched exposure is applied to the xyz of both constants at their four
RENDER-THREAD consumers, not at the main-thread fill (s1-adapted-scene-scale 8.3):
  - CHWShader_D3D::mfSetParameters, the ECGP_PB cases (fog pass, forward PB path)
  - CVolumetricFogStage::FillForwardParams (forward cbFog)
  - CVolumetricCloudsStage::GenerateCloudShaderParam (clouds fog themselves from
    this buffer; RenderCloud is a compute pass with no per-view CB, so a
    shader-side PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX would silently read 1.0 there)
  - CWaterStage::UpdatePerPassResources (cbVoxVolFog)
.w is an anisotropy term and is untouched. Exactly 1.0 off the switch.

Also found and fixed on the way: the volumetric clouds' SKY light
cb.skylightRayleighInScatter (the dome's horizon Rayleigh radiance, engine units)
was unexposed while shadeColorFromSun was - a cloud's sky-lit half did not follow
the aperture.

Overlay, so this cannot hide again. The coverage line's hard-coded "sky YES" is
replaced by a measured line (y=215) from CSkyStage::SSceneReferredDebug, filled
from the constants the pass actually uploads: the technique that ran
(Nishita/skybox), the factor the dome constants were multiplied by, the dome
straight up in UNEXPOSED cd/m2 (CPU evaluation of texel 0 with SkyPassPS's own
arithmetic), its value in the target and stops vs grey, the sun texel after the
peak cap, the cap, and "far plane = vol-fog inscatter" when volumetric fog is on.
"metered EV: -28.49" was log2(1e-12): the histogram path publishes the scalar
meter as 0 by design; the line now prints the camera's MeterTargetEV ("histogram
band") or "n/a" with the reason.

Not changed, deliberately: the Manual EV clamp at 24 (saturation 2e7 cd/m2, nine
stops over sunlit snow - nothing in a scene needs more once the sky follows), and
the sky peak cap, which is already computed in unexposed units and pre-exposed
with the writer clamp as the fp16 guard only.

Notes: research/s8-fog-and-clouds.md 2.1/2.6 corrected, research/s8-nishita-sky.md
section 7, decisions/s8-metering-sky.md and research/s8-metering-sky.md (Sky
Weight treated a symptom), decisions/s1-writer-coverage.md post-mortem,
STRUCTURE.md two rows, log.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HXzRVK4yBVDUNfdWXEwV5y
